WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.400
-Martin, welcome --
-How's it going, man?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.634
-Martin, welcome back
to the show.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:04.968
-Thank you for having me.
-We love having you on.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.434
I got this date correct,
I believe.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:10.200
August 27, 1992, 30 years ago,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.667
you created Martin Lawrence --
you created "Martin."

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:13.934
[ Laughter ]
Sorry.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.501
No, you didn't create
Martin Lawrence.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.701
You came out as a baby
and got your own sitcom.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.367
No, you created "Martin."
-Yes.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.334
-30 years later, did you think
that it would still be --

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.734
have such an impact
on pop culture?

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.000
-I had no idea.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.100
-I just knew every year
we got picked up,

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.000
we were just trying to make
the show work.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.567
And to know that it's still
running 30 years later,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.834
I'm just over the moon, man.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.501
I feel truly blessed.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:41.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.400
You know, I was going to ask
you, when you're out in public,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.934
what -- you've got
so many catchphrases,

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.100
but what do people
yell at you the most?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.701
-"Whuzzah!"
-Yeah! There you go.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.567
-Or they might go,
"You go, boy!"

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.868
-"You go, boy." Yeah.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:56.534
-They'll flip the "you go, girl"
and go, "you go, boy."

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.601
-Yeah. "Damn, Gina."
-"Damn, Gina."

00:00:58.601 --> 00:00:59.801
-Yeah, you so crazy.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.067
Yeah, and that stuff, oh, yeah.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.868
You know, there's only a handful
of people -- I was looking at

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:06.167
a list today -- that have
successful sitcoms with

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.267
their name in it.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.634
-You know, with "Martin."

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.767
When you were selling
or creating the show,

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.934
did you ever have
any other titles?

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.834
-Nah, I always wanted it
to be "Martin."

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.801
I knew other comedians had shows
after their name.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:21.400
So I was like,
"I want it to be 'Martin.'"

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.634
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.834
Now y'all know me as Martin.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.801
-"Martin!"
-"Martin!"

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:29.334
Exactly right.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:33.234
You had a bunch of famous,
famous iconic cameos

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:34.634
when you did the show.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.234
I thought it would be fun to
maybe show a picture

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.434
and you can tell me
what you remember

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.400
from that scene or that time.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.267
Alright, ready? Check this out.
-Alright.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.701
-My man Snoop.
-It's Snoop Dogg.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.133
-Yeah.
-With Jerome.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.734
-With Jerome, yeah.
-With Jerome, yeah.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.400
What do you remember about
Snoop Dogg coming on?

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.934
-I remember Snoop -- this was
his first time on TV.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.267
-It was?
-So he was shy.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.601
He was really shy.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:57.901
But he was just real cool
and down-to-earth.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.033
And he kept it real.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.734
-He just kept it Snoop
all the way.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.133
-Did he laugh? Did he break?

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:05.701
-He -- He -- In his own way,
but it was Snoop style.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.400
-Yeah, exactly.
-Snoop style, yeah.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.734
But he was a lot of fun
to have on the show.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:12.801
-Okay. How about this?
I like this here.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.200
-Ah, Jackie Chan. Yeah.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.701
-Jackie Chan.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.300
He appears himself.
He was a love interest.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.467
Do you remember this?

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.667
-To Sheneneh.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.434
-How do you sell him on that?

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.634
-We made up that episode.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.701
But see, the reality was me
and Jackie Chan

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:33.267
were supposed to do "Rush Hour"
together and, you know,

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.667
but they didn't have
enough money for me.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:43.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:45.467
So that didn't happen.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.767
So Jackie came on the show,
you know,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.868
just to come and support
the show.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.667
-And when did they film
"Rush Hour"?

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.534
-When they got Chris Tucker.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:56.868
A year later.
-Yeah, a year later.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.334
-That's wild.
Alright, how about this?

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.834
We know and love this man.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.701
This is Tracy Morgan.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.267
-Yeah, my man Tracy.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.667
-Hustle Man.
-Hustle Man.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.434
-This is before he was
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.434
and he always gives you credit
for his big break.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:13.767
-Yeah. What I first saw Tracy
on "Def Jam,"

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:18.434
and he pulled up his shirt and
he start patting his stomach,

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:21.434
and I just said,
"This boy is wild, man."

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.467
I said, "If I ever get my show,
I gotta put him on the show."

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:27.267
And when I put him on the show,
he was just so quick

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.968
and so natural and spontaneous
and just --

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:32.200
I mean, just a gem to have
on the show.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.534
-Right? Yeah, he is.
-Really is.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:36.434
-And this last one.
This is just one of the coolest.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:37.767
I know he's one of
your favorites.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.434
Here's you and Richard Pryor.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.534
-Yeah, my idol, Richard Pryor.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:45.934
Yeah.
-Wow. Wow.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.467
-Richard Pryor and Eddie Murphy
are the reasons I do comedy.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.400
-He's the reason I do
stand-up comedy.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.467
[ Applause ]
-I mean, what was it like?

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.901
Did you know him at all
off-stage as well?

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.834
-I didn't know him off-stage.

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:00.667
This was the first time
I got to meet him.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.167
And it was just an honor

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.267
and it was lot of fun
to have him there.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.100
-That's the coolest thing.
Anyway, I just figured it would

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.367
be fun to go through that stuff.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.601
I was saying to you backstage

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.968
that I was such a fan
of the show.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:13.000
Me and my friends would wear
"Martin" T-shirts.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.434
-Yeah.
-And you was like, "Yeah, you

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.434
can still get them if you go to
shopmartinlawrence.com.

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.133
-Yes.
-You got all sorts of --

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.734
-All sorts of stuff you can get,

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.667
and I would love to see y'all
in them.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.701
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.567
Also, the "Martin" swag.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:29.033
You even have -- I don't know
if you know this came out,

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:31.367
but the "Martin" trivia game.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:34.133
This is a card game you can play
with your friends.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:37.501
And I know that Questlove is
a big "Martin" fan.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.033
-And congratulations, Quest
on your Oscar, brother.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.434
-Thank you, brother.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.601
Thank you.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.701
-"Summer of Soul."

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.734
"Summer of Soul," you did
your thing, brother.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:49.601
Did your thing.
-That's pretty cool.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.534
Quest, I thought it'd be,
if it's okay with you,

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.634
maybe I could ask you a few
"Martin" trivia questions.

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.501
-Okay.
-And see how you do. Alright?

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:56.667
-I got this.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.033
-Do you really think
you got this?

00:04:58.033 --> 00:05:00.501
-I do.
I watched the entire canon.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.467
After I won the Oscar,
I went on break.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.501
I watched the entire five-season
canon in a row.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.534
On vacation.
-Gosh!

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:09.701
-I got this.
-Wait, wait.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.234
Alright, so you're recently --

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:12.868
you're recently up to date
on "Martin."

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.033
-I'm addicted to this show. Yes.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.334
-Yeah, me too. I love him too.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.601
Alright, here we go.
Ready for this one?

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:20.701
What gift did Gina receive
from Martin by mistake

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.968
instead of the diamond earrings?

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.567
-By mistake?
-By mistake.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.501
-Ah, 'cause I knew he got
his grandmom's duvet.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:31.367
I think he gave her Jerome's
gold tooth by accident.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.501
[ Ding! ]
-That would be it!

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.634
That would be it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:38.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.200
-And how Jerome's gold tooth --

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:45.534
-We did an episode where they
went to the club Shiznit.

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:47.000
[ Laughter ]
Shiznit.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.067
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:51.868
-Probably couldn't even get away
with that now. Oh, my God.

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:54.467
Shiznit.

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:57.334
Oh, my gosh.
Alright, that's good.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:58.701
You're one for one.
Alright, ready?

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:02.567
How about this? Which
celebrity -- [ Laughs ]

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.934
-What, what, what?
-I remember this one.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:08.801
Which celebrity impersonator
punched Martin in the face

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:10.434
when they went to Hollywood?

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.200
I remember this one.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.467
Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:16.234
-"Whoa!" Michael Jackson.

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.367
-There you go. That's right.
[ Ding! ]

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.400
That was funny.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.033
Michael Jackson punched you.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:23.434
Did you ever hang out
with Michael?

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:25.100
Did you ever meet Michael?

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.934
-I met Mike years ago
at an awards show.

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:32.167
And it was the weirdest thing
because he wanted to meet me

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:35.300
and they called me and brought
me to his dressing room.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.734
And I went in the dressing room.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.167
And when I went in, his mother
was in there

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.534
and he just looked at me
and went --

00:06:40.534 --> 00:06:44.567
[ High-pitched laughing ]

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:46.067
-Started laughing.

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.534
-That's all he did.
-That's all he did?

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:48.667
-That's all he did.
-Alright.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.801
-And I felt awkward
'cause I was like --

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.133
-What are you going to do?
-"I gotta go.

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:54.234
Nice to meet you, Mike."

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:55.501
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:57.033
And did he laugh again
when you left?

00:06:57.033 --> 00:06:58.701
-[ High-pitched laughing ]
-Yeah, he did on the way out.

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:00.133
Amazing.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:04.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:06.300
Alright, Quest, last one.
Here you go.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.267
What was the name of Martin's
restaurant

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.467
that opened and closed
in the same day?

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:12.133
-Ah! "Rent 'em spoons."

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:17.667
It is Marty Mart's Meatloaf
and Waffles Joint.

00:07:17.667 --> 00:07:20.734
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:23.133
-Meatloaf and waffles.

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:25.334
I want to talk about
the "Martin" reunion special

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:27.567
when we come back. More with
Martin Lawrence after the break.

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:28.801
The reunion!

